== 9. What this does and does not establish ==================== 
  WHAT THIS DESIGN REMOVES, relative to bulk cohorts: 
    - tissue composition: both compartments lie in one section and 
      share the same stroma 
    - between-patient variation: the comparison is paired 
    - patient covariates: age, sex, Breslow and site are constant 
      within a patient and cancel 
    - our own judgement about which spots are which: the labels are 
      the authors' published assignments 
    - culture artefact: this is tissue, not a cell line 
 
  WHAT REMAINS A LIMITATION: 
    - a 55 um spot holds several cells, so a 'nevus' spot is 
      nevus-DOMINATED, not pure, even above the purity threshold 
    - their object retains an uneven fraction of spots per section 
      (14.9% to 99.5%), consistent with depth filtering; this costs 
      precision but is symmetric within each patient's pair 
    - all lesions are WHO class I low-CSD melanoma, median Breslow 
      1.05 mm, so this is nevus versus EARLY melanoma and not 
      melanoma generally 
    - section 4 describes where the gene sits in intact skin; it is 
      descriptive and not a test 
  no warnings raised 
